-- Typechecks cleanly; none of the three #ASSERTs can be decided. A bare assumed
-- BOOLEAN is neither TRUE nor FALSE: `#ASSERT NOT b` forces b and RAISES (stuck
-- on an assumed term), while `#ASSERT b`, and `#ASSERT TRUE AND b`, which is just
-- b, reduce to the symbolic b WITHOUT raising. All three must report the same
-- undecided outcome.
ASSUME b IS A BOOLEAN
#ASSERT b
#ASSERT NOT b
#ASSERT TRUE AND b
